@namespace NSail.Components

@* One row of tools above the grid — a flexible child (search Grow or NsSpacer) pushes the
   rest to the right. Used inside NsPageHeader; not meant to stand alone in a page. *@
@* A TOOL NEVER GIVES UP ITS CONTENT WIDTH — the row WRAPS, the same answer the title row one
   level up gives (NsTitleBar, nsail#1869). Without it a no-wrap row has only flex-shrink left
   when the tools outgrow the width, and shrinking a button wraps the LABEL inside it with the
   glyph parked between the two lines (Importar Feriados nacionales on a phone); with it an
   action that no longer fits takes a line of its own, whole. The search zone is the one child
   that declares a width it may give back (ns-toolbar-search's flex: 0 1 22rem), so it is still
   what squeezes first and the wrap costs the row nothing where the tools already fit. *@
<NsStack Horizontal Wrap Align="NsAlign.Center" Justify="NsAlign.End" Gap="NsSize.Sm" Class="@Class">
    @ChildContent
</NsStack>

@code {

    [Parameter]
    public RenderFragment? ChildContent { get; set; }

    [Parameter]
    public string? Class { get; set; }
}
